# A mission founded at a Tupi camp, then two turns of native relations (Iroquois gift).
# Start: turns_spring_1600_events' output (France, Spring 1600, turn 108) re-saved once; fixture: every
# French unit with no orders / go-to / pioneer job on sentry, and the Free Colonist #123 in Quebec
# (45,24) made a Missionary (type 3) with no orders and full moves, the active unit.
# Turn 108: the Missionary walks to (44,23) and into the Tupi camp (tribe 30, 43,23): Establish
# Mission founds "Sainte Marie de Quebec" (mission byte 1 = France; Tupi friction for France 6 -> 0).
# Turn 109 end: the Iroquois bring 16 Ore to Port au Prince (@INDIANGIVESTUFF, stock[6] 0 -> 16).
# England (at war with France) captures Guadeloupe meanwhile.
key KP_7                 # turn 108: Missionary NW to (44,23)
wait 6
key KP_4                 # W into the Tupi camp: Establish Mission / Incite Indians / Cancel Action
wait 6
key Return               # Establish Mission (row 0)
wait 6
key Return               # "Sainte Marie de Quebec mission founded": End of Turn
wait 6
key space                # end turn 108
wait 30
key Return               # Colonization Help: Time Scale
wait 10
key Return               # (AI turn still running; presses between popups are ignored)
wait 10
key Return
wait 10
